    "criticism": "Step 3 performed a naïve HTML scrape that counted every <img> tag on the page, including navigation icons, logos, thumbnails from external sites, and images that belong to the Wikipedia interface rather than the article itself.  The code did not restrict the search to the article body (e.g., the \"mw-parser-output\" container), nor did it filter by image type or by whether the image is part of the article’s content.  Moreover, it used the current revision of the page instead of the specific 2022 revision requested.  These omissions caused the count to inflate to 28 instead of the correct 13.  A correct implementation would fetch the 2022 revision via the Wikipedia API, parse only the article body, and count only images that are part of the article content (e.g., images with the class \"thumbimage\" or those inside the infobox and gallery sections)."
